# object: bench
# name: Timber bench
# model: bench.glb
# note: Backrest is at -Z, so a sitter faces +Z.

collide circle 0.55 at -0.6 0
collide circle 0.55 at 0.6 0
# **One seat, not two.** The bench is 1.66 wide and the Postmaster is 1.34, so a
# pair at either end put her overhanging the slats with nowhere for a second
# sitter to go.
# 
# Both numbers are measured off the mesh, not estimated: the slats top out at
# 0.78 and the backrest sits at z -0.23, and her hips ride 0.3 above her own
# origin in the seated pose. 0.78 - 0.3 = 0.48 puts her on the slats rather
# than through them, and +0.06 clears the backrest.
seat middle at 0 0.48 0.06
interact sit middle sit down
